    body: pair("Pest pressure usually rises for a reason.\n\nPlants under stress. One crop dominating the ground. Or broad chemical use that has already removed the predators that were helping you.\n\nSo before you treat anything, look at the whole system.\n\nIs the plant short of water? Is the soil compacted, or hungry? Are predators already working on the problem for you?\n\nA yellow leaf is not automatically an insect. It can be water, nutrition, or root damage. Find out which before you act.\n\nWork through four steps, in order.\n\nOne. Observe. Look at the damage pattern, the underside of the leaf, the stem, and the plants nearby.\n\nTwo. Check for stress. Soil moisture, roots, spacing, nutrition, drainage.\n\nThree. Protect what's helping you. Beneficial insects are doing work you'd otherwise do yourself.\n\nFour. Only then, act — and start with the lightest thing that works. Physical removal, barriers or changes in crop care may help. Check that the action suits the problem and monitor the result.\n\nIf a treatment is needed, use a product registered for that crop and pest, and follow its label. This includes neem products. Check protection and harvest waiting instructions. Do not improvise mixtures or stronger doses.\n\nBe honest with yourself about which step you usually skip.", "Pest pressure i anzela u engedzea nga tshiitisi.\n\nZwimela zwi re na stress. One crop dominating the ground. Kana broad chemical use yo no bvisa predators dze dza vha dzi tshi ni thusa.\n\nNgazwenezwo, ni sa athu u thoma u lafha tshithu, sedzani system yoṱhe.\n\nNaa tshimela tshi khou shaya maḓi? Mavu o compacted kana a si na pfushi? Predators dzi khou shuma kha thaidzo iyi dzi tshi ni thusa already naa?\n\nYellow leaf a i ambi automatically uri ndi insect. Zwenezwo zwi nga vha maḓi, nutrition, kana u vhaisala ha midzi. Wanani uri ndi zwifhio ni sa athu dzhia vhukando.\n\nTevhelani vhukando vhuṋa nga u tevhekana.\n\nTsha u thoma. Sedzani. Sedzani damage pattern, tlhelo ḽa fhasi ḽa ḽiṱari, tsinde, na zwimela zwi re tsini.\n\nTsha vhuvhili. Sedzani stress. Soil moisture, midzi, spacing ya zwimela, nutrition na drainage.\n\nTsha vhuraru. Tsireledzani zwine zwa khou ni thusa. Beneficial insects (zwikhokhonono zwine zwa thusa) zwi khou ni itela mushumo une na inwi na vha ni tshi ḓo u ita.\n\nTsha vhuṋa. Ndi hone fhedzi ni tshi dzhia vhukando — thomani nga the lightest thing that works. Physical removal, barriers kana tshanduko kha nḓila ya u ṱhogomela zwimela zwi nga thusa. Ṱolani arali vhukando vhu tshi tea thaidzo, ni bvele phanḓa ni tshi sedza mvelelo.\n\nArali treatment i tshi ṱoḓea, shumisani product registered for that crop and pest, nahone ni tevhele label yayo. Hezwi zwi katela neem products. Ṱolani protection and harvest waiting instructions. Ni songo ḓiitela misanganedzo kana stronger doses.\n\nNi ḓi ambele ngoho nga ha vhukando vhune na anzela u vhu pfuka."),
